Exclude MinGW from upstream's WIN32 timespec substitution. Winsock's struct timeval
carries a 32-bit long tv_sec on LLP64 while MinGW's default time_t is __int64, so with
the substitution in force src/readcdf.c:244 -- the one call site not behind CDF_DEBUG or
TEST_TIME -- hands cdf_ctime's const time_t * parameter the address of a 32-bit field.
MinGW-w64 declares a struct timespec whose tv_sec is already a time_t, so excluding it
needs nothing else. Upstream's __DJGPP__ block below is left alone.

diff --git a/src/cdf.h b/src/cdf.h
--- a/src/cdf.h
+++ b/src/cdf.h
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 #ifndef _H_CDF_
 #define _H_CDF_
 
-#ifdef WIN32
+#if defined(WIN32) && !defined(__MINGW32__)
 #include <winsock2.h>
 #define timespec timeval
 #define tv_nsec tv_usec
